title: "A rigorously characterized I3322 quantum wall and finite-dimensional nonattainment"
type: article
authors:
  - given-names: Seth
    family-names: Douglas
    email: apsiape@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"
version: 1.1.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Apsiape/i3322-exact-wall"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21782008"
abstract: >-
  The tensor-product and commuting-operator suprema of the canonical I3322
  Bell functional are identified with a rigorously characterized domain-wall
  constant, and neither model has a finite-dimensional maximizer. Consequently,
  C_q(3,3;2,2) is nonclosed and is minimal by input counts among bipartite
  binary-output scenarios where nonclosure can occur.
keywords:
  - Bell inequalities
  - I3322
  - quantum correlations
  - commuting operators
  - computer-assisted proof
  - nonattainment
  - nonclosed quantum correlations
  - minimal Bell scenario
